cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  To cite verifiable.pro as a whole, use these metadata. To cite one article or page,
  give its title, its address on verifiable.pro (not the address of its Markdown source),
  its filing or update date and the date you read it.
title: "verifiable.pro: bilingual reporting on verifiable AI systems"
abstract: >-
  verifiable.pro reports in English and Simplified Chinese on verifiable AI: evidence that
  lets someone other than an AI provider check the provider's claims, such as which model
  answered a request or which software handled it. Coverage starts from trusted execution
  environments (TEEs), remote attestation and confidential computing. It compares them with
  other ways to check a claim: zkML, verifiable inference and formal verification check
  computations and code, while AI evaluations, audits, model signing and supply-chain
  provenance check models and their origins. The comparison also extends to content
  credentials (C2PA) and watermarking, agent accountability and the verification of AI
  governance commitments. The site publishes news briefs, analysis, explainers and guides, a
  resource library and a glossary, and lists the SHA-256 digest of every published source in
  a manifest that anyone can recompute.
# The Citation File Format offers only "software" and "dataset"; the work cited here is the
# site's articles, pages and data files, so "dataset" fits better than "software".
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: verifiable.pro
    website: "https://verifiable.pro/"
url: "https://verifiable.pro/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sept-usc/verifiable-pro"
keywords:
